closure label, ghc_hs_iface,"] [74 3 "// stable_ptr_table (rtsapi.go)"] [88 2 "// NODES.adjust: \"STUB INDEX\" a line, the parameter of the x86-64 adjustor's return address (bin/lib/hsi/check)"] [108 2 "// a function the C calls and neither it nor musl defines: hsi's own when its table has it (the RTS's API a test's C"] [109 2 "// calls: hs_free_stable_ptr, getProgArgv, ...)"] [124 1 "// ciClone is ci's __clone, which cloneMachine's wrapper calls; cloneMachine is the machine whose C is loaded."] [128 1 "// hookClone wraps ci's __clone (musl's pthread_create starts a thread through it) so that the machine knows the threads"] [129 1 "// its C starts (queue 430): cIdle lets them run while no Haskell thread can."] [145 1 "// RunC runs a -no-hs-main program (HES60 (a)): its C main through musl's __libc_start_main, which calls exit(main(argc,"] [146 1 "// argv, envp)); the C calls hs_init, its foreign exports (rts_inCall) and hs_exit, which flushes the Haskell handles as"] [147 1 "// hs_exit does. The status is the C's exit status."] [165 1 "// hsExit is hs_exit: the standard handles flushed (on a thread of their own, as shutdown's), the C finalizers run."] [172 3 "// the threaded RTS's hs_exit (exitScheduler, threaded.go): the other threads deleted, those in safe foreign calls"] [173 3 "// left to return into a stopped RTS (conc059), where the non-threaded RTS's waits for them"] [182 1 "// cStack is an initial stack's vector as Linux's (ci's RunMain's): argv's pointers, 0, the environment's, 0, the"] [183 1 "// auxiliary vector (AT_PAGESZ, AT_RANDOM); the environment's address and argv[0]'s."] [209 1 "// cFunc is the C program's function named s when it defines one (code, or a native ci has)."] [221 1 "// cResolve is the C function a static foreign call of s calls when the C program has it and hsi's table does not, or"] [222 1 "// it is one of cFirst's."] [230 1 "// cFuncAt is the C program's function at address a, or nil."] [242 1 "// cCall calls f with the machine's argument values (an integer kind or an address as an integer, a float or a double as"] [243 1 "// a floating value) and returns its result in the representation res."] [270 1 "// cCallArgs calls f on ci's main thread."] [275 1 "// cNative makes hsi's C function fn at address a a native of ci's program: its arguments as the machine's values."] [280 1 "// cBridge makes f, a function of ci's program, call hsi's fn."] [304 1 "// cLabel is the address of the C program's object or function s, when it has one."] [318 1 "// cFlush flushes C's stdio at the program's end (libc's exit, after the Haskell handles' flush)."] [326 1 "// cValue is the value of the C program's object s in the representation res, when it has one: a capi import of a value"] [327 1 "// (foreign import capi \"h.h value i\"), whose wrapper GHC's C compiler makes and hsi reads as the object itself."] [351 1 "// identity is the word that stands for a heap object in memory C reads (an Array# argument's elements): a pinned byte"] [352 1 "// array's address, an integer itself, else an address of an unmapped region, one per object, kept for the run."] [377 1 "// identBase is the region of objects' identities: no mapping of crt's is there."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[55 20] [60 24] [62 29] [65 29] [66 46] [67 26] [75 24] [76 53] [90 44] [94 39] [112 29] [117 34] [138 23] [150 20] [309 25] [312 43] [369 25]]} (go/file "cprog.go" :imports [


